<title>USA: CCC buys 15,000 T US sorghum for export to Africa.</title>
<headline>CCC buys 15,000 T US sorghum for export to Africa.</headline>
<dateline>CHICAGO 1997-02-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Commodity Credit Corp of the U.S. Department of Agriculture said Thursday it had bought 15,000 tonnes of U.S. sorghum for export to Uganda and Ethiopia, March 1-25 shipment.</p>
<p>The total comprised 10,000 tonnes from Farmland Industries for Ethiopia at a cost of $111.08 per tonne, FOB Galveston and 5,000 tonnes from ADM/Growmark for Uganda at a cost of $113.26 per tonne, FOB Ama.</p>
<p>((Chicago newsdesk 312-408 8720))</p>
</text>
